{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1377-fan-written-scion-material","id":1377,"title":"Fan-Written Scion Material","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-02T16:38:38-07:00","id":1377,"title":"Fan-Written Scion Material","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fan-Favorite Non-Canon PDFs and Other Fun Files</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Charts and References</b></span><br /> <b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/?g994hu2c1p8fuqa\" target=\"_blank\">Scents of the Divine Index</a></b> - A compiled list of all canon and many non-canon Scents for easy reference. (by Telgar)<br /> <b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?1j17mec6lhlcwyz\" target=\"_blank\">Associated Powers Index</a></b> - A big list of all the Epic Attributes and Purviews along with which deities are Associated with each one. Canon-only. (by Telgar)<br /> <b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?i4y4cbb346o4l12\" target=\"_blank\">Divine Nouns</a></b> - A list of how to refer to singular and plural deities of the various Pantheons. (by Telgar)<br /> <b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?5lvs85ef68c5vdl\" target=\"_blank\">Knack Charts</a></b> - Flowchart of all the canon Knacks. (by Telgar)<br /> <b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?cb8nv1r3n3cwj18\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Quick-Reference Chart</a></b> - Tables listing the Associated and Favored traits of most of the non-canon Gods listed in this thread. (by Telgar)<br /> <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15pTG0lqJ1rtf_OylBjbNvmTjVP_dPSHkT-Zuk2GFaFk/edit?hl=en_US#bookmark=id.kd57d9lkbc0w\" target=\"_blank\">Fan-Written PSP Quick-Reference Chart</a></b> - Quick-refernece for fan-written PSP's. (by Telgar)<br /> <b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/?cv8p9wdk29y0ut4\" target=\"_blank\">Titanic Templates</a></b> - Cliff-Notes of all 10 official + 10 fan-written Titan Templates (by Telgar)<br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/iq3b4fm3oawmtsv/Scion%20-%20Armory%20v1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Scion Armory</a></b> (link broken?) - Illustrated table of various modern and historical weapons from the Scion Corebook. (by Kalle)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Extra Gods</b></span><br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?8qo887vr8ef898t\" target=\"_blank\">Additional Gods</a></b> - extra gods for all Pantheons (by Demonchilde)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?b9nnir3a93sc5ab\" target=\"_blank\">Additional Gods 2</a></b> - Compiled list containing (most of) the gods written up on the Official Scion Wiki. (multi-author document)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?gcjcrcg7kgzbea4\" target=\"_blank\">Additional Gods 3</a></b> - Collection of Gods from several different Pantheons. (by Sorcerymon)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?29eval99z96d4ix\" target=\"_blank\">Additional Canon Gods</a></b> - A compiled list of the extra canon Gods that are scattered around the various books. (by Telgar)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?0003kec6icl9xsx\" target=\"_blank\">Combined Additional Gods</a></b> - This document combines all the above documents and includes a few new Gods. However, duplicate Gods were removed. (multi-author document)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>New Pantheons and sub-Pantheons</b></span><br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.4shared.com/document/MxNRuP6n/The_Atua_v3-_Final.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Atua</a></b> - Maori / Polynesian Pantheon (by Ptah1888 and Pashupatastra)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?jmrua7oujp7kgb6\" target=\"_blank\">The Vanguard of Avalon</a></b> - Arthurian Pantheon (by BlaineTog)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?p430ep0f7pp8tn9\" target=\"_blank\">The Vairgit</a></b> - Arctic Pantheon (by TerriblyUncreative)<br /> \u2022<a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?1j3duikkv46f2a6\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Rus</b></a> - Slavic Pantheon (by Demonchilde)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?2hnc3grwv8kchfk\" target=\"_blank\">The Anunna</a></b> - Mesopotamian Pantheon (by Demonchilde)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?9oc1uyy5156qre1\" target=\"_blank\">The Manitou</a></b> - Native American Pantheon (by Demonchilde)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?0dhxvbbixko7qvc\" target=\"_blank\">Sub-Pantheons</a></b> - Several small groups of Gods that fall under the political aegis of larger Pantheons. (by Demonchilde)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?vilq6la83aue8lu\" target=\"_blank\">The Vanir</a></b> - Norse sub-Pantheon (by Telgar)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?tvxrxzvfuvv9dht\" target=\"_blank\">The Aisar</a></b> - Etruscan sub-Pantheon of the Dodekatheon (by Telgar)<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">New or Revised Purviews</span></b><br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"https://mega.co.nz/#!4lU0WB5D!SWlYaUyTv5lTgv0NNNupmDIJTVhl8zMwerKrA1gIxT4\" target=\"_blank\">Alternate Arete</a></b> - A single-purchase version of Arete. (by ArthurH3535)<br /> \u2022<a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?rbdm42u8fxr6uej\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Alternate Prophecy</b></a> - a conversion of Prophecy into an All-Purpose Purview, with distinct Boons for each level. (by R_B_Bergstrom)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?brk13cte42sd8rm\" target=\"_blank\">Emotion Purview</a></b> - an All-Purpose Purview to control emotions, differentiated like Animal, by specific manifestation. (by Brent-not-Broken)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?ddbrqzsbquv5dwy\" target=\"_blank\">Atman</a></b> - a replacement PSP for the Devas. (by Brent-not-Broken)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?4g0oo59750osnet\" target=\"_blank\">Jotunblut</a></b> - a revised Jotunblut, focusing on gaining giant-like traits and power. (by Brent-not-Broken)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?vu3gf4j4q6liakg\" target=\"_blank\">Tsukumo-Gami</a></b> - a revised PSP for the Amatsukami. (by Brent-not-Broken)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?ks764dpqcd93bfb\" target=\"_blank\">Forge Purview</a></b> - A Purview for crafters and artificers of all kinds! (by Telgar)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?zyaq1n0iqk4t0uy\" target=\"_blank\">Slavic Pantheon-Specific Purview: Prav</a></b> - Prav empowers a Slavic Scion when he follows his Virtues. (by Telgar)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?btfze1s7jool2zo\" target=\"_blank\">Sound Purview Revised</a></b> - A Purview for singers, storytellers, screamers and speech-makers. (by Telgar)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l_eJiTmqnd3rJ2rknRhHyRGelUZGc136PlzZm6n-jMw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Animal</a></b> - A version of Animal that is suitable for hunting Gods and has no Animal (Species) divisions. (by Iry)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rLFF53CaSnRwC0dnLwDgfa_ojSnJkSxQVFepqsyUZSU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Roman Pantheon-Specific Purview: Civitas</a></b> - The Roman Gods are at their strongest when working together for the common good.<br /> <b>\u2022<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N72vYdif3cWRyZJW0kdnZ2j_klC7B32cDrH_W49EEuI/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Gaulish Pantheon-Specific Purview: Deuogdonio</a></b> - Gaulish sacrifices can harvest strength from defeated foes.<br /> <b>\u2022<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZCCy7qFYRPb6sroa4UEeyWNswR0pNWzv659CJVY61QA/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Etruscan Pantheon-Specific Purview: Nethsrac</a></b> - Gods of the Etruscans make their will known through visions and portents.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Pantheon-Specific Resources</b></span><br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?6w1k0na8qh872pz\" target=\"_blank\">Aztec Resource Double Whammy</a></b> - A combination PDF that has both Brent-Not-Broken's Atzlanti Toolkit and Griffinguy24's Nagual Animal Companion resources! (by Brent-not-Broken and Griffinguy24)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Antagonists and Titans</b></span><br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?3zhzsr380zr55bd\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Titans</a></b> - New Titan Avatars, creatures and other assorted information. (by Pashupatastra)<br /> \u2022<b><a href=\"http://multiverse-crisis.wikidot.com/munera\" target=\"_blank\">Munera, Titan of Decadence</a></b> - A wiki-page detailing the Titan of Decadence and its Avatars. (by Kizuna Wave)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 09-22-2015, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:01:13-08:00","id":4380,"title":"","content":"I ran a campaign loosely rooted in Neil Gaiman's American Gods. It quickly spiraled far from that tree. The game's website has some NPCs, purviews, knacks, and more.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/scion/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/scion/index.htm</a><br /> <br /> The index page never stayed up to date with story posts. Those are here (in doc and pdf form): <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/scion/campaign/newsletter/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/scion/campaign/newsletter/</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:31:09-08:00","id":8555,"title":"","content":"I'll link those on the Fan Sites list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T14:36:24-08:00","id":45852,"title":"","content":"Updated today, adding three old PSPs of mine for the Etruscan, Roman and Gaulish Gods.<br /> The Etruscan PSP is a working draft, not a polished product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T18:29:06-08:00","id":46656,"title":"","content":"I need to PDF my 'updated' Alternate Arete. Because I'd read something totally wrong about how spending a Legend to reroll worked. The base rules actually made 1/2 of 'canon' Arete totally stupid...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b